From: Zinc
Subject: [PATCH] qtfb: let a client dock its window under xochitl's header

MESSAGE_SET_WINDOW_STATE gains WINDOW_STATE_DOCKED (3): the window
fills the screen below xochitl's top header, without a window bar,
showing the framebuffer below that height 1:1; the header stays
xochitl's own, live. Visibility reports 3 while docked, capability bit
2 (CAPABILITY_DOCKED) announces it, and the new
STATE_CHANGED_REASON_INSETS (3) gives the client the header's height,
in the initial state packets and whenever it changes.

The header's height is read from xochitl's live item tree (the tallest
item spanning the screen's width at its top, 48 to 240 px), or from
dock.json in AppLoad's directory, else 120 px.

The header belongs to xochitl: a press on it reaches xochitl and
minimizes the docked window; when that press opened a popup (the
sidebar, a menu) the window docks again once it is closed.
---
